        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Delmer Daves, Jean-Pierre Jeunet, Lou Edelman, Frank Borzage\n- Works: Flirtation Walk, Delicatessen, The City of Lost Children, Amélie\n- Roles: screenwriter, director, producer\n- Topics: film\n\nFacts:\n- Delmer Daves was born on July 24, 1904, and he was an American screenwriter, director, and producer.\n- Flirtation Walk is a 1934 romantic musical film written by Delmer Daves and Lou Edelman and directed by Frank Borzage.\n- Jean-Pierre Jeunet was born on 3 September 1953, and he is a French film director and screenwriter.\n- Jean-Pierre Jeunet is known for the films Delicatessen, The City of Lost Children, and Amélie.\n- Delmer Daves died on August 17, 1977.",
